0 A low mounting board carries corrugated pipes in arches, straight spans and an upright loop.
0 Name: HOSE_FLEXIBLE_8.5L-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Holly Wood
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Blue and yellow tubes rise in short humps from a small plate-built rack. Brown and orange samples extend farther outward, including an upright stem with a loop beside it.
0 // Rigid construction: Wing plates, ordinary bricks and 4070 headlight bricks create the mounting positions. The loose hose and end-piece samples compare fittings with tabs and without tabs.
0 // Build lesson: Choose the end fitting and its direction before shaping a pipe. Small side-facing bricks can turn a flat base into a convincing pipe or cable test fixture.
0 // Reuse: The upright loops are posed shape examples, not evidence that the hose supports itself or that every illustrated fitting is interchangeable.
